Clarification: 

sed -n '1~7,+4p' filename
1. To print 5 lines and then skip 2 lines repeatedly, use:

sed -n '1~7,+4p' filename

This prints:

Lines 1–5
Skips lines 6–7
Prints lines 8–12
Skips lines 13–14
Continues the same pattern


